    "reasoning": "All 16 answers are mathematically correct and supported by their own captured worked solutions. q-69476: substituting u=8x cancels the factor 8 and gives arcsec(8x)+C on |8x|>1. q-114035: substituting u=√5 x gives arctan(√5 x)/√5+C. q-102799: y=1/2 and x=-3/2; the selected inverse-matrix expression evaluates to this solution vector, with its displayed x understood as vector notation. q-76069: the denominator is 4(x-2)², so continuity holds exactly for x≠2. q-12283: the unit square's image has area |4·4-3·2|=10. q-88206 and q-88582: both integrands are even, so each symmetric integral equals twice its integral over the positive half-interval. q-19302: v(t)=2t-2+1/t, giving v(3)=13/3≈4.33. q-73136: the chain rule gives v(t)=2t/(t²+1). q-115810: numerator and denominator have opposite signs when x<5/4 or x>3. q-88655: opposite signs occur exactly between -1 and 3. q-115858: x² is positive wherever defined; the numerator is nonpositive when x≤-7/2 or x≥3, including both roots. q-38509: factoring the numerator as (x+2)(2x-3) gives positive intervals (-2,0) and (3/2,∞). q-84841: the graph has equation (y+3)²=x-1; the selected parameterization satisfies it and covers the entire parabola. q-106464: the selected parameterization gives (y-5)²=t²=2(x-2) and covers the entire parabola. Its extra spacing commands are equivalent to the source form. q-85077: the inverse matrix gives (13,-5), and multiplying by T returns (1,-2). No submitted grade is supplied; confirmation is based on the captured worked solutions.",
